क्रुश् क्रो॑शति क्रो॑श˚ते pp. क्रुष्ट (w. act. & pass.
mg) cry out, shout, croak, lament;
 call to (acc). — अनु shout at
(acc.);
 C. show sympathy (lit. follow in lamenting). अभि call or cry
at (acc.), lament, mourn. आ call aloud, scold at, revile, defame;
challenge, emulate. उद् cry out, call to (acc.). उप show anger or
defiance. प्र raise a cry, call at (acc.). वि the same. सम् cry
out together, shout angrily at (acc.). — Cf. अपक्रुष्ट, आक्रुष्ट,
उपक्रुष्ट.

क्रूर॑ a. bloody, raw, sore;
 cruel, harsh, dreadful. n. a
wound or sore;
 bloodshedding, slaughter;
 cruelty, harshness.
